      "content": "The IRS understands that home offices are used for various things, but for tax deductions, you must demonstrate that the expense is *ordinary and necessary* for your business. Since the chair is primarily for your design work, using it occasionally for personal television viewing is unlikely to negate the business deduction. Maintain clear records showing how the chair supports your professional design operations to keep your documentation sound.",
      "source": "target",
