    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i think i'll just keep the receipt and log a percentage of use if needed. another thing though—i've noticed some small discrepancies in my bank reconciliations lately. like, small amounts of money just seem to be \"off\" or missing from my digital logs compared to my actual statements. i haven't found a pattern yet, it's just these tiny, random gaps. is that common for freelancers or is it a sign i'm doing something wrong with my accounting?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those small, unaccounted-for discrepancies can be very common, especially with digital banking, as they might be small bank fees or automated transactions you haven't noted. It's prudent to thoroughly review all digital statements against your QuickBooks entries to pinpoint the source of the variance. If the gaps persist, it might indicate a missed recurring charge or a small processing fee that needs to be logged as an expense.",
